# Auto commit and push

After finishing a coherent set of changes in this repository, **always create a git commit and push to `origin`** without waiting for the user to ask.

Follow the usual commit protocol (status, diff, log, HEREDOC message, then `git push`).

Commit author for this project (do not leak a local personal identity):

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="linux-proton-drive contributors"
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="contributors@users.noreply.github.com"
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="linux-proton-drive contributors"
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="contributors@users.noreply.github.com"
```

Skip commit only if there is truly nothing to commit. Do not force-push unless the user explicitly requests it.
